* Activity is the ticket's at-a-glance progress: one line per entry, shown on its board card, in a conductor's Tickets tab, in search and in its Activity tab. A note there (\`post_note\`) covers what changed since your last note or submit. Each Activity entry SHOULD be one short line, 400 characters or less, so it scans quickly: what you changed and why ("I changed X because Y"). Activity shows only the first line; anything after it sits behind Show details, which the human may never open, so the first line MUST say what happened on its own. It MUST NOT explain, list options or repeat the spec or earlier activity; reasoning MUST go in the spec or stay in the transcript. Every new spec revision adds its own Activity entry, with the note you gave \`edit_spec\` as its line, so write that note by the same rules and don't repeat it with \`post_note\`; \`post_note\` is for progress the spec doesn't show.

