1. In the worktree (/Users/me/.harness/worktrees/NYT-3), make sure there are no uncommitted changes; commit any that belong to the work to \`harness/nyt-3\`.
2. Merge \`harness/nyt-3\` into the base branch \`main\`, working from wherever \`main\` is checked out, never in the ticket's worktree. Find it with \`git -C /Users/me/Sites/nyt worktree list\`:
   * \`main\` is checked out in a worktree (the main checkout at /Users/me/Sites/nyt, or another one): merge there with \`git -C <that path> merge harness/nyt-3\`.
   * \`main\` isn't checked out anywhere: when it can fast-forward, update it without a checkout: \`git -C /Users/me/Sites/nyt fetch . harness/nyt-3:main\`. Otherwise add a temporary worktree (\`git -C /Users/me/Sites/nyt worktree add <temporary folder> main\`), merge there, and remove that temporary worktree afterwards.
3. Resolve trivial conflicts yourself (lockfiles, formatting, adjacent edits). If a conflict needs a real decision, run \`git merge --abort\`, leave both branches as they were, and say so.
4. After a successful merge, remove the worktree (\`git -C /Users/me/Sites/nyt worktree remove /Users/me/.harness/worktrees/NYT-3\`), and delete the merged branch from the worktree that has \`main\` checked out (\`git -C <that path> branch -d harness/nyt-3\`, before removing a temporary worktree): \`-d\` checks the branch against what is checked out where it runs. After a fast-forward without a checkout, confirm it with \`git -C /Users/me/Sites/nyt merge-base --is-ancestor harness/nyt-3 main\`, then \`git -C /Users/me/Sites/nyt branch -D harness/nyt-3\`.

