exports[`built-in run prompts reviewPrompt · round 1, no baseline 1`] = `
"Review NYT-3 "Add dark mode".

## Spec (revision 3)
Read it first with \`read_spec\` { revision: 3 }: the work was submitted against that revision. Revisions never change once written, so it reads the same however long the review takes, even if someone edits the spec meanwhile.

## Spec changes since the human approved it
There is no approved baseline (the ticket started without planning), so judge the spec as written.

## Activity so far
(none)

\`get_ticket\` { key: "NYT-3" } has the full Activity and the stored path of each attachment the spec shows. Verify the work yourself, then call \`review_decision\` exactly once."
`;

exports[`built-in run prompts reviewPrompt · round 1, spec untouched since the baseline 1`] = `
"Review NYT-3 "Add dark mode".

## Spec (revision 3)
Read it first with \`read_spec\` { revision: 3 }: the work was submitted against that revision. Revisions never change once written, so it reads the same however long the review takes, even if someone edits the spec meanwhile.

## Spec changes since the human approved it
None: the spec is still revision 3, as the human approved it.

## Activity so far
* note, agent: Toggle wired up
* submitted, agent: Toggle done; tests pass

\`get_ticket\` { key: "NYT-3" } has the full Activity and the stored path of each attachment the spec shows. Verify the work yourself, then call \`review_decision\` exactly once."
`;

exports[`built-in run prompts reviewPrompt · round 2, with a baseline diff and earlier rounds 1`] = `
"Review NYT-3 "Add dark mode": round 2, a re-review.

## Spec (revision 3)
Read it first with \`read_spec\` { revision: 3 }: the work was submitted against that revision. Revisions never change once written, so it reads the same however long the review takes, even if someone edits the spec meanwhile.

## Spec changes since the human approved it
Revision 2 is what the human approved by pressing Start:
\`\`\`diff
--- spec rev 2
+++ spec rev 3
@@ -1,1 +1,1 @@
-Status: not started
+Status: done
\`\`\`

## Earlier review rounds
Round 1: changes requested at commit 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567.
The toggle forgets its state.
Also the icon.

This is round 2. Focus on what changed since the last round: \`git diff 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567..HEAD\`. Confirm each point from the last round was addressed, and check the rest only for regressions.

## Activity since the last review
* message, human: Use localStorage
* submitted, agent: Persisted the toggle

\`get_ticket\` { key: "NYT-3" } has the full Activity and the stored path of each attachment the spec shows. Verify the work yourself, then call \`review_decision\` exactly once."
`;

exports[`built-in run prompts completePrompt · checkout (no worktree) · instructions undefined 1`] = `
"NYT-3 "Add dark mode" is approved. Finalize it.

There is no ticket branch or worktree to merge. Do the wrap-up in the instructions below; if there are none, confirm the working tree is in a sensible state and stop.

When you are finished, call \`post_note\` with what you did."
`;

